{"_v":1,"id":"mamma-mia-west-end-2021","bd":{"positive":5,"mixed":1,"negative":0},"rv":[{"cn":"Veronica Lee","o":"The Guardian","s":93,"b":"Rave","t":1,"u":"https://www.theguardian.com/stage/theatreblog/2009/apr/07/mamma-mia-abba-musical","d":"2009-04-07","q":"Ten years on, Mamma Mia! – a love story set to Abba songs – still doesn't rival Sophocles, but it remains as stonkingly, wonderfully, unbelievably good as the first time I saw it."},{"cn":"Jessie Thompson","o":"Evening Standard","s":86,"b":"Rave","t":1,"u":"https://www.standard.co.uk/go/london/mamma-mia-musical-theatre-tickets-in-london-a3705346.html","d":"2017-11-29","q":"It's a riotously fun musical packed with hits that offers a bonding evening for mothers and daughters everywhere."},{"cn":"Owen Gleiberman","o":"Variety","s":71,"b":"Positive","t":1,"u":"http://‘Mamma Mia!’ Review: A Revival of the 2001 Jukebox Musical Offers Another Undiluted Shot of ABBA Joy. Only It’s Now a Double Layer Cake of Nostalgia","q":"I saw the original stage version three times, and while the revived “Mamma Mia!” has its own spirit (which I would call slightly more bumptious, with more aggressive choreography), it’s really the same show. It’s directed, like the original (..."},{"cn":"Alan Bird","o":"London Theatre","s":82,"b":"Positive","t":2,"u":"https://www.londontheatre.co.uk/reviews/mamma-mia-review","d":"2022-01-25","q":"The mixture of Abba songs, camp dance routines, platform boots and Lycra costumes based around a soppy romance comedy script creates a delightful evening of sheer fun and pleasure."},{"cn":"Nina Caplan","o":"Time Out London","s":77,"b":"Positive","t":2,"u":"https://www.timeout.com/london/theatre/mamma-mia","d":"2017-03-21","q":"Given the songs, a story just about solid enough to stay upright on its platform heels, and a Greek island setting perfect for a whimsy of this sort, it's impossible not to fall for 'Mamma Mia!'s twinkling charms."},{"cn":"Alice Jones","o":"The i","s":62,"b":"Mixed","t":2,"u":"https: